      <p class="msc-section-kicker">Bitcoin Ecosystem</p>
      <h1>How Bitcoin Marketplaces Work</h1>
      <p class="msc-learn-page__deck">A Bitcoin marketplace connects buyers and sellers around offers, listings, payment conditions, and delivery. The marketplace may coordinate discovery, messaging, price formulas, escrow, reputation, dispute resolution, or custody, but those functions are separate and should be evaluated individually.

Bitcoin can settle one leg of a marketplace trade. It does not verify a listing, prove that an off-chain payment or product was delivered, reverse a mistaken transfer, or decide a dispute. Understanding the complete trade path reveals which promises come from Bitcoin and which depend on software, counterparties, operators, and law.</p>
